  "term": "hypothalamic–pituitary–adrenal axis",
  "definition": "The hypothalamic–pituitary–adrenal axis is the body’s stress axis, a linked system involved in responses to psychological challenges and traumatic events. In this packet, its activity is reflected by cortisol levels and is discussed as a possible pathway connecting stress with cellular aging.",
