      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims the HPAA is involved in responses to “psychological challenges,” but the packet describes associations with “psychological challenges, including traumatic events” only in the context of the hypothesis about traumatic events (child mortality) and cellular aging; it does not specifically establish “psychological challenges” as a documented, supported role of the HPAA beyond that phrasing.",
        "It also describes HPAA as a “linked system,” while the packet refers to the “hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis (HPAA), or stress axis” but does not explicitly characterize it as a “linked system.”",
        "The remaining parts are broadly supported: the packet assesses HPAA activity via cortisol levels and discusses HPAA activity as mediating links between a traumatic event (child mortality) and a cellular aging marker (telomere length)."
